# Boneyard layout skeletons

**Canonical home** for skeleton policy — other rules link here; do not duplicate loading-skeleton guidance elsewhere.

See also: **`error-handling.mdc`**, **`async-ui.mdc`**, **`page-layout.mdc`**, **`design-tokens.mdc`**. Index: [`skills/SKILL.md`](../../skills/SKILL.md).

**Default:** use **shadcn `Skeleton`** (`@/components/ui/skeleton`) unless layout fidelity is worth the extra setup.

**`LayoutSkeleton`** (`@/components/ui/layout-skeleton`) wraps real UI and shows auto-captured bones. Use it on **primary data surfaces** where a polished loading state matters (main list on a page, hero card block) — not every spinner in the app.

## When to use which

| Case | Use |
| ---- | --- |
| Main list / card on a page | `LayoutSkeleton` + `fixture` |
| Nested tab, refetch shimmer, one-off block | shadcn `Skeleton` — **simpler** |
| Tiny chip / single line | shadcn `Skeleton` |
| Capture path is awkward (deep route, many states) | shadcn `Skeleton` — don't add dev-only pages or extra infra |

**Do not** hand-stack shadcn blocks to fake a complex list — either use `LayoutSkeleton` or one shadcn block as a coarse placeholder.

## Setup (template defaults)

1. `boneyard-js` in `dependencies`
2. `boneyardPlugin({ out: "./src/bones" })` in `vite.config.ts` — **dev only** (`command === "serve"`)
3. `import "./bones/registry"` in `src/main.tsx` and `src/test/setup.ts`
4. `boneyard.config.json` at repo root
5. `@/components/ui/layout-skeleton` wrapper

Commit `src/bones/*.bones.json` + `registry.ts`. Production never runs Playwright.

## Component pattern

Put `fixture` on the **same component** as the real children — inline mock data is fine; no separate dev routes or fixture pages.

```tsx
const LIST_FIXTURE = [{ id: "1", label: "Row one" }, { id: "2", label: "Row two" }];

<LayoutSkeleton
  name="examples-list"
  loading={listStatus === "loading"}
  ariaLabel="Loading examples"
  fixture={<ExamplesList items={LIST_FIXTURE} />}
>
  {listStatus === "ready" ? <ExamplesList items={data!.items} /> : null}
</LayoutSkeleton>
```

Keep **error** / **empty** as siblings — not inside `loading={true}`.

## Capture

- Vite plugin captures from **`/`** on dev start and HMR — skeleton must mount on a route the crawler hits.
- Off-home skeletons: run `pnpm exec boneyard-js build http://localhost:5173` while that page is reachable, **or** use shadcn there instead.
- Missing bones → `LayoutSkeleton` shows its `fallback` (muted pulse block) — acceptable in dev.

## Anti-patterns

```tsx
// Bad — dev-only BonesPage / fixture routes just for capture
<Route path="dev/bones" element={<AllSkeletonsFixture />} />

// Bad — Boneyard for a single gray bar
<LayoutSkeleton name="x" loading fixture={...}><div className="h-8" /></LayoutSkeleton>
// Good
<Skeleton className="h-8 w-full" />
```

## Checklist

- [ ] Only primary surfaces use `LayoutSkeleton`; rest stay shadcn.
- [ ] `fixture` lives next to the component — no extra pages.
- [ ] `src/bones/registry` imported in `main.tsx` + test setup.
- [ ] Bone JSON committed when capture is done.
